    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0248" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg174"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Sir F. Bruce</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 14, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir;</hi> I have been requested by the president of
                    the Soldiers’ National Cemetery, at Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, to extend to you
                    an invitation to attend the ceremonies of laying the corner-stone of the
                    monument to the memory of the soldiers who fell on the battle-field of
                    Gettysburg, which are to take place on the 4th of July next.</p>
                <p>The ceremonies cannot fail to be interesting, and it is hoped that you may find
                    it convenient to accept the invitation to be present on that occasion.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir Frederick W. A. Bruce</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
